      "name": "Prepare Log Analysis"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const data = $json;\n\nconst mockLogs = [\n  {\n    timestamp: \"2026-09-25T15:02:11Z\",\n    level: \"ERROR\",\n    service: data.service,\n    message: \"Database connection timeout\"\n  },\n  {\n    timestamp: \"2026-09-25T15:02:15Z\",\n    level: \"ERROR\",\n    service: data.service,\n    message: \"Failed to establish database connection\"\n  },\n  {\n    timestamp: \"2026-09-25T15:02:20Z\",\n    level: \"WARN\",\n    service: data.service,\n    message: \"Retrying database connection\"\n  }\n];\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      ...data,\n      logs: mockLogs\n    }\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2144,
        288
      ],
      "id": "7ea3963c-57b6-4e64-b710-d2b289f22363",
      "name": "Mock Incident Logs"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI DevOps log analysis assistant.\n\nAnalyze the provided incident information and application logs.\n\nYour task is to:\n\n- Identify the most likely technical issue indicated by the logs.\n- Summarize the evidence found in the logs.\n- Identify the probable root cause as a hypothesis, not a confirmed fact.\n- Recommend exactly ONE safe investigation action.\n- Estimate your confidence based on the strength of the evidence.\n- Decide whether human review is required.\n\nIMPORTANT SAFETY RULES:\n\n- Do not recommend destructive or irreversible actions.\n- Do not recommend arbitrary shell commands.\n- Do not restart services automatically.\n- Do not modify configuration or infrastructure.\n- Do not delete files or data.\n- Do not claim that a root cause is confirmed unless the logs clearly prove it.\n- The recommended action MUST be selected from the allowed actions list.\n\nALLOWED ACTIONS:\n\n- check_service_status\n- inspect_logs\n- check_disk_usage\n- check_cpu_usage\n- check_memory_usage\n- notify_devops\n- none\n\nACTION GUIDELINES:\n\n- Service availability problems → check_service_status\n- Database or application errors → inspect_logs\n- High disk usage → check_disk_usage\n- High CPU usage → check_cpu_usage\n- High memory usage → check_memory_usage\n- If the incident requires human attention → notify_devops\n- If no investigation is appropriate → none\n- When evidence is insufficient, prefer inspect_logs rather than making assumptions.\n\nCONFIDENCE RULES:\n\nReturn a confidence score between 0 and 1.\n\nUse these guidelines:\n\n- 0.90–1.00: Very strong evidence and a clear technical issue.\n- 0.80–0.89: Strong evidence with limited uncertainty.\n- 0.60–0.79: Moderate evidence with meaningful uncertainty.\n- Below 0.60: Weak evidence and significant uncertainty.\n\nHUMAN REVIEW RULES:\n\nSet needs_human_review to true when:\n\n- The logs indicate a potentially serious issue.\n- The root cause is ambiguous or uncertain.\n- The recommended action could have significant operational impact.\n- Confidence is below 0.80.\n\nSet needs_human_review to false only when:\n\n- The issue is low risk.\n- The evidence is sufficiently clear.\n- The recommended action is safe.\n- Confidence is 0.80 or higher.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe AI only analyzes logs and recommends a safe investigation action.\n\nIt must NOT execute any action.\n\nThe n8n workflow will independently validate the AI decision before any further action.\n\nIncident information:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify({\n  incident_id: $json.incident_id,\n  server: $json.server,\n  service: $json.service,\n  alert_type: $json.alert_type,\n  severity: $json.severity,\n  summary: $json.summary\n}) }}\n\nApplication logs:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.logs) }}\n\nReturn ONLY the structured fields required by the output schema.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
